Z||000004||Sanfran||06-03-2001||01:14 AM||||They are extremely hard to come by now.  I just sold one to a guy on the forum.  Gtquik I believe his name was.  It was a Hooker and I had a hard time finding one.  I sold it after I put a 2.8 in mine.  You do notice soem extra power when installed in the Duke.<BR>Hooker don't make them anymore and u have to find them used.<P>Good luck on finding one.  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1626330&a=12427866&p=45623747"> <BR>'86 2m4 <BR>Modified w/V6||||reg||1
Z||000005||kslish||06-03-2001||02:55 AM||||I've got this header for my 2m4, but haven't installed it yet because I haven't gotten around to getting it coated in Cermakrome.<P>The Hooker part number for the Fiero exhaust header is 4703 (or 4703-1 for the ceramic coated version).<P>Summit (www.summitracing.com) lists the following prices on the headers:<P>HOK-4703    HEADER PONTIAC           $276.99<P>HOK-4703-1  PONTIAC HDR 4 CYL CTD    $458.39<P>They are listed as a special order item.<P>I ordered and recieved mine last year, and they are still listed in the current Hooker Header catalog.<P>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR> <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||DecadenceR||06-03-2001||10:46 AM||||Okay, thanks a lot for the info.<BR>Now I can get that done within the next month!!!<BR>Ken, does that include the downpipe to the cat? Or would I have to purchase that extra?||||reg||1
Z||000007||kslish||06-03-2001||04:37 PM||||Here is a pic of the header (this is the ceramic coated version):<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.acrnet.com/eric_nancy/Hooker1.JPG"> <P>As you can see it runs practically all the way to the catalytic converter.  At worst, you would probably only need a short adapter pipe to run it all the way to the converter.<P>A concern with this header...it runs pretty close to the starter, and starters don't like heat.  A starter heat shield is a basic requirement (that is another reason I am getting my header coated...it should help with the heat issue).<P>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR> <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||DecadenceR||06-03-2001||06:40 PM||||Niiiiiiiiiice....<BR>Thanks!!!||||reg||1
Z||000009||TRiAD||06-03-2001||06:50 PM||||Summit has hi-flo CATs for $100. <P>Good luck!<P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> ||||reg||7
